{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>You and your sons and your father's house.</b> The meaning of <b>your father's house</b> — it appears to me that it refers to Moses, who is from his father's house, for the warning came upon him as well, for if it were about the Kohathites, they are the same as the rest of Israel regarding entry into the Mishkan of HaShem. Further, from what it says immediately afterward, ״וְגַם אֶת אַחֶיךָ בְנֵי לֵוִי״ etc., it indicates that until now He was not speaking about them. Rather, it appears that the meaning of <b>your father's house</b> is Moses, like the one who says (Zevachim 102b) that the priesthood never ceased from Moses; and even according to the one who says that Moses was not consecrated as a priest except during the seven days of inauguration, I hold that he was not prohibited from entering the place where the priests tread. And our Rabbis, of blessed memory, said (Sifrei) — and this is their language: ״בֵּית אָבִיךָ״ — these are the Levites; this teaches that the Levites are warned by means of the priests — this far is their language. And this is the way of midrash, to derive in the verse the laws that they had from Sinai." "<b>with you, etc.</b> One needs to know why it says <b>with you</b> after it explicitly mentioned Aaron. And perhaps it comes to say that they are warned together at all times, lest you say there is a time when Aaron is liable and a time when his sons are liable — Scripture says <b>with you</b>, to say that they are warned together at all times."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {0 "Reading המשכן as 'the Mishkan' (Tabernacle); the phrase מקום דריסת רגלי הכהנים refers to the area within the sanctuary where priests alone may walk."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:10:55.414425270Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}